{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7e224fa1a781a907","name":"card_unit_p_40b_tomahawk","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Allegiance/units/card_unit_p_40b_tomahawk","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"P-40B TOMAHAWK","text":"Infantry units you deploy or add get +1+1.","flavorText":"The P-40B Tomahawk was an American fighter and ground attack aircraft used during WWII by many Allied air forces. The Soviet military and naval air forces received 247 P-40Bs from the Americans through the Lend Lease agreement. The aircraft were shipped from Great Britain or from the US and many of them arrived incomplete and had to be assembled in the USSR. Soviet test flights showed some defects in test flights, but the Tomahawks were nevertheless used right away in front line services. The P-40Bs were a good match against the German BF 109s, the range and fuel capacity was superior to most of the Soviet fighters, but the biggest complaint was about its poor climb rate and problems with maintenance. The P-40 was mostly used by the Soviet Air Force in 1942 and early 1943, but after that many of them were replaced with the Soviet Lavochkin La-5 and Yakovlev fighters.","faction":"Soviet","type":"fighter","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_p_40b_tomahawk","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_p_40b_tomahawk_title","SourceString":"P-40B TOMAHAWK","LocalizedString":"P-40B TOMAHAWK"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_p_40b_tomahawk_text","SourceString":"Infantry units you deploy or add get +1+1.","LocalizedString":"Infantry units you deploy or add get +1+1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_p_40b_tomahawk_history","SourceString":"The P-40B Tomahawk was an American fighter and ground attack aircraft used during WWII by many Allied air forces. The Soviet military and naval air forces received 247 P-40Bs from the Americans through the Lend Lease agreement. The aircraft were shipped from Great Britain or from the US and many of them arrived incomplete and had to be assembled in the USSR. Soviet test flights showed some defects in test flights, but the Tomahawks were nevertheless used right away in front line services. The P-40Bs were a good match against the German BF 109s, the range and fuel capacity was superior to most of the Soviet fighters, but the biggest complaint was about its poor climb rate and problems with maintenance. The P-40 was mostly used by the Soviet Air Force in 1942 and early 1943, but after that many of them were replaced with the Soviet Lavochkin La-5 and Yakovlev fighters.","LocalizedString":"The P-40B Tomahawk was an American fighter and ground attack aircraft used during WWII by many Allied air forces. The Soviet military and naval air forces received 247 P-40Bs from the Americans through the Lend Lease agreement. The aircraft were shipped from Great Britain or from the US and many of them arrived incomplete and had to be assembled in the USSR. Soviet test flights showed some defects in test flights, but the Tomahawks were nevertheless used right away in front line services. The P-40Bs were a good match against the German BF 109s, the range and fuel capacity was superior to most of the Soviet fighters, but the biggest complaint was about its poor climb rate and problems with maintenance. The P-40 was mostly used by the Soviet Air Force in 1942 and early 1943, but after that many of them were replaced with the Soviet Lavochkin La-5 and Yakovlev fighters."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Trig